id: pm-igdvfq
title: "GH-1004: history-repair remains writer-version-specific across 2026.8.7 and 2026.8.13"
description: "A real post-epoch reproduction shows genuine drift repaired by pm 2026.8.7 is accepted only by that reader, while repair by 2026.8.13 is accepted only by the newer reader; alternating the supported CLIs rewrites the same stream indefinitely and each reports the other's bytes as hash/chain drift."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:history",compatibility,history-repair,regression
created_at: "2026-08-14T01:58:48.803Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T10:15:01.221Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: A cross-version fixture reproduces the two-writer loop; repair converges or refuses without rewriting an internally consistent supported epoch; diagnostics attribute version incompatibility instead of generic corruption; focused and repository-wide exact coverage remain green
parent: pm-4jk8kx
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: "On one drifted tracker, alternate published 2026.8.7 and 2026.8.13 history-repair --all, running each version's health --strict-exit after each rewrite as documented in GitHub #1004."
expected_result: Supported readers either accept one converged repaired representation or the repair command refuses a writer-version-only rewrite with an actionable compatibility diagnostic.
actual_result: "Repair under 2026.8.7 makes 2026.8.13 fail strict health; repair under 2026.8.13 makes 2026.8.7 fail, and the files differ byte-for-byte."
affected_version: 2026.8.13
component: history hashing and repair compatibility
regression: true
customer_impact: Pinned CI and global agents can disagree on identical bytes and repeatedly rewrite append-only evidence while following the documented remediation.
